On-device model
---------------
- Wake phrase model: sherpa-onnx-streaming-zipformer-small-ru-vosk-int8-2025-08-16
  (converted from alphacep/vosk-model-small-streaming-ru) — Alpha Cephei and
  k2-fsa — Apache License 2.0. Downloaded by the build (SHA-256 pinned) into
  assets/wakeword/phrase/.
- omni_v0.2fp.onnx (wake word «Омни» / «Omni») — a small classifier head
  trained for this project with the openWakeWord v0.6.0 training stack
  (dscripka/openWakeWord code, Apache 2.0; vendored/adapted train code in
  training/oww_train.py). Training data, all with licenses that allow
  commercial use:
  * synthetic speech generated with Piper TTS (OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl, used only
    as an offline tool, its code and output are not shipped) from these
    voices of rhasspy/piper-voices (license of the underlying corpus, per the
    voice MODEL_CARD): ru_RU-denis and ru_RU-dmitri (OHF-Voice/voice-datasets,
    CC0), en_GB-vctk (CSTR VCTK, 109 speakers, CC BY 4.0), kk_KZ-raya and
    kk_KZ-iseke (IS2AI Kazakh TTS, CC BY 4.0);
  * recordings of the project owner's own voice (own data, consent given);
  * synthetic noise only (no third-party noise or speech corpora).
  Voices with non-commercial, research-only or unverified licenses were
  excluded from data and tests (en_US-l2arctic, en_US-ryan, tr_TR-dfki,
  ru_RU-ruslan: CC BY-NC(-SA); en_US-lessac: Blizzard 2013 research license;
  ru_RU-irina, en_GB-jenny_dioco, en_GB-alan, en_US-amy and others: license
  unknown or non-standard). Metrics and provenance: training/OMNI_V0.2FP_REPORT.md.
  The CC BY corpora require attribution, given here: VCTK (Yamagishi et al.,
  CSTR, University of Edinburgh), Kazakh TTS corpora (IS2AI, Nazarbayev
  University).
  The earlier model omni_v0.1.onnx is no longer distributed: it was trained on
  Piper voices whose commercial-use terms are not confirmed.
- openWakeWord frontend models (melspectrogram.onnx, embedding_model.onnx,
  v0.5.1) — dscripka/openWakeWord — reused as the acoustic frontend; the
  embedding network comes from Google's speech_embedding (TF Hub), Apache
  License 2.0. Bundled under app/src/main/assets/wakeword/. The openWakeWord
  pre-trained WAKE-WORD models (e.g. hey_jarvis) are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and are
  therefore not distributed with the app. SHA256 pins: see SHA256SUMS in the
  same directory.
- Gemma (on-device LLM used via MediaPipe, optional user-installed model) is
  governed by the Google Gemma Terms of Use and Gemma Prohibited Use Policy:
  https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
  The model weights are NOT distributed with this repository; the user
  supplies them and is responsible for complying with Gemma terms.

